WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:07.063
"Anti-Inflammatory Benefits of Berries"

00:00:07.063 --> 00:00:10.560
A study following 10,000
Norwegian men for 40 years

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:12.180
found that those
eating berries

00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:13.500
more than 14 times a month

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:16.560
were more likely to be alive
at the end of the study.

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:18.900
Higher intake of anthocyanins,

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:20.940
the brightly colored pigments
in berries,

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:23.700
has been associated with
anti-inflammatory effects,

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:26.400
but these are all
just associations.

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:28.320
You can't prove
cause and effect,

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:31.500
until you put it
to the test.

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:34.260
A double-blind, randomized,
placebo-controlled study

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:35.820
found that blueberry smoothies

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:37.860
could turn off
inflammation genes.

00:00:37.860 --> 00:00:41.580
This is measuring the expression
of pro-inflammatory genes

00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:43.620
in white blood cells
taken from individuals

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:46.920
before and after six weeks

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:50.220
of drinking placebo smoothies
with no blueberries.

00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:51.780
They got worse over time.

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:53.280
Six weeks later,

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:55.500
more inflammatory chemicals
pouring out,

00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:58.920
whereas the blueberry group
started out about the same

00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:02.220
at week zero, but six weeks
of daily blueberries

00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:04.020
and the expression
of inflammatory genes

00:01:04.020 --> 00:01:06.300
such as IL-6 went down.

00:01:07.620 --> 00:01:11.820
Strawberries,
sweet (Bing) cherries,

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:17.040
black raspberries,
extracts of goji berries,

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:22.020
and Indian gooseberries (amla)
have also been shown

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:25.440
to decrease inflammatory markers
in interventional trials.

00:01:25.980 --> 00:01:28.380
Have people eat
a largely unhealthy breakfast,

00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:29.940
including a bagel
with cream cheese,

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:31.620
margarine, egg,
and a glass of milk,

00:01:31.620 --> 00:01:34.500
and the rise
in C-reactive protein and IL-6

00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:35.760
over the subsequent six hours

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:39.780
was less when just 10 grams
of strawberry powder,

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:41.400
equivalent to
five large strawberries,

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:43.920
was added to the meal.

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:47.580
A cup of blueberries
was able to significantly blunt

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:49.920
the IL-6 spike
after a ham and cheese sandwich,

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:52.500
and the same with two cups
of raspberries

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:54.480
versus a sausage
and eggs breakfast.

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:58.620
The same amount of banana,
however, was no match,

00:01:58.620 --> 00:02:01.200
unable to stop a tripling
of IL-6 levels

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:02.340
within four hours.

00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:06.300
Why did the raspberries work,
whereas bananas didn't?

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:09.660
Maybe it's the antioxidants.

00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:13.620
Free radicals can disfigure
proteins in our bodies

00:02:13.620 --> 00:02:16.080
to the extent
they become unrecognizable

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:17.340
by our immune systems

00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:19.620
to the point that our body
attacks them as foreign.

00:02:20.520 --> 00:02:23.820
The inflammatory autoimmune
response this triggers

00:02:23.820 --> 00:02:25.440
may be prevented, however,

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:29.820
by saturating our bodies
with sufficient antioxidants.

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:33.900
Food selection based on high
total antioxidant capacity

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:35.880
improves endothelial function.

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:37.920
High-antioxidant fruits
and vegetables,

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:39.420
such as berries and greens,

00:02:39.420 --> 00:02:42.480
have been found to douse
systemic inflammation

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:46.680
significantly better
than the same number of servings

00:02:46.680 --> 00:02:49.320
of more common low-antioxidant
fruits and veggies,

00:02:49.320 --> 00:02:50.880
such as bananas and lettuce.

00:02:51.780 --> 00:02:52.980
What about apples?

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:56.160
Not only associated
with all sorts of benefits

00:02:56.160 --> 00:02:57.300
in observational studies

00:02:57.300 --> 00:02:59.580
but proven
to improve risk factors

00:02:59.580 --> 00:03:01.080
in randomized
controlled trials,

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:04.440
including inflammation,
but the data is mixed.

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:08.460
Six months of a half cup a day
of dried apple rings

00:03:08.460 --> 00:03:11.040
significantly lowers CRP levels,

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:13.860
though the same drop happened
in the control group,

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:16.380
who instead ate about
half a cup of prunes a day.

00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:20.580
Freeze-dried apple powder
flopped completely.

00:03:20.580 --> 00:03:23.820
Eating three
fresh Gala apples, however,

00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:25.860
appears to lower inflammation
both acutely,

00:03:25.860 --> 00:03:28.260
within six hours,
and over time.

00:03:29.160 --> 00:03:33.060
Six weeks of three Galas a day
lowered fasting levels of IL-6,

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:37.680
though four weeks of twice
as many Shampion variety apples,

00:03:37.680 --> 00:03:39.840
a cross between Cox
and Golden Delicious,

00:03:39.840 --> 00:03:42.060
didn't seem to have any effect.

00:03:42.900 --> 00:03:45.600
What about grapes
for inflammation?

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:47.520
Neither raisins
nor powdered grapes

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:48.420
appeared to help.

00:03:48.420 --> 00:03:51.660
What about drinking berries?

00:03:51.660 --> 00:03:53.880
Sipping red wine
for 6 to 12 weeks

00:03:53.880 --> 00:03:56.040
did not affect
lower inflammation,

00:03:56.040 --> 00:03:59.700
compared to gin, water,
or abstention, and acutely,

00:03:59.700 --> 00:04:02.100
two to three glasses
of red or white wine

00:04:02.100 --> 00:04:03.480
can make things worse,

00:04:03.480 --> 00:04:06.360
increasing IL-6 levels
by about 50 percent

00:04:06.360 --> 00:04:10.080
within six hours compared
to a nonalcoholic beverage.

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:14.340
However, red or purple
grape juice may help.

00:04:14.340 --> 00:04:17.940
Antioxidant supplements
failed miserably.

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:20.340
No anti-inflammatory benefit
was found

00:04:20.340 --> 00:04:22.080
for antioxidant vitamins
and minerals

00:04:22.080 --> 00:04:24.660
like vitamins C, E,
beta-carotene, or selenium,

00:04:24.660 --> 00:04:28.320
which brings us back
to the bright red, blue,

00:04:28.320 --> 00:04:30.720
purple anthocyanin
plant pigments.

00:04:30.720 --> 00:04:33.360
Dozens of randomized
controlled trials

00:04:33.360 --> 00:04:36.360
on anthocyanin-rich supplements,
mostly berry extracts,

00:04:36.360 --> 00:04:39.960
have demonstrated
anti-inflammatory effects.

00:04:39.960 --> 00:04:42.660
This may be why
red-fleshed plums

00:04:42.660 --> 00:04:44.760
beat out
yellow-fleshed apricots

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:46.800
in reducing CRP blood levels.

00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:50.460
Or, why even super healthy
fruits like mangoes

00:04:50.460 --> 00:04:52.980
may be powerless
against the inflammation

00:04:52.980 --> 00:04:55.140
caused by
a Sausage and Egg McMuffin,

00:04:55.140 --> 00:04:58.920
whereas a half dozen studies
combined show pomegranates,

00:04:58.920 --> 00:05:01.500
a fruit packed with
ruby red anthocyanins,

00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:04.920
can bring down inflammation
over time.

00:05:06.060 --> 00:05:09.360
The anti-inflammatory effects
of berries are so potent

00:05:09.360 --> 00:05:11.340
you can feel it
if you push yourself.

00:05:11.340 --> 00:05:15.120
Check out my video Reducing
Muscle Soreness with Berries.

00:05:15.720 --> 00:05:18.720
As I note in Watermelon
for Sore Muscle Relief,

00:05:18.720 --> 00:05:20.640
eating two cups of watermelon

00:05:20.640 --> 00:05:22.620
prior to
intense physical activity

00:05:22.620 --> 00:05:26.220
was also found to significantly
reduce muscle soreness.

00:05:26.820 --> 00:05:29.520
The researchers concluded
that functional compounds

00:05:29.520 --> 00:05:32.040
in fruits and vegetables
can "play a key role

00:05:32.040 --> 00:05:35.040
in the design of new natural
and functional products,"

00:05:35.040 --> 00:05:37.740
but why design new products

00:05:37.740 --> 00:05:40.800
when nature has already designed
everything you need?

00:05:41.400 --> 00:05:44.040
Unfortunately, chronic
watermelon consumption,

00:05:44.040 --> 00:05:45.480
giving people
a whole watermelon

00:05:45.480 --> 00:05:47.400
and a gallon bag
of precut watermelon

00:05:47.400 --> 00:05:48.480
every week for 12 weeks,

00:05:48.480 --> 00:05:51.420
did not seem to affect
levels of inflammation.

00:05:52.380 --> 00:05:54.360
Optimizing recovery
from exercise

00:05:54.360 --> 00:05:58.020
is considered the holy grail
of exercise science,

00:05:58.020 --> 00:06:00.060
but what about
discernable effects

00:06:00.060 --> 00:06:03.360
on inflammatory conditions
such as arthritis?

00:06:04.020 --> 00:06:07.380
Tart cherries may be helpful
in treating gout.

00:06:08.040 --> 00:06:10.980
Delicious dietary treatments
are much welcomed,

00:06:10.980 --> 00:06:14.460
as some gout drugs
can cost $2,000 a dose,

00:06:14.460 --> 00:06:16.440
carry no clear-cut distinction

00:06:16.440 --> 00:06:19.560
between nontoxic, toxic,
and lethal doses,

00:06:19.560 --> 00:06:21.540
or can cause a rare side effect

00:06:21.540 --> 00:06:24.840
in which your skin
detaches from your body.

00:06:25.980 --> 00:06:28.320
Of course,
the best way to deal with gout

00:06:28.320 --> 00:06:30.540
is to try to prevent attacks
in the first place

00:06:30.540 --> 00:06:34.500
with a more plant-based diet
and lower alcohol consumption.

00:06:36.300 --> 00:06:38.220
Strawberries were pitted against

00:06:38.220 --> 00:06:40.320
the most common
inflammatory joint disorder,

00:06:40.320 --> 00:06:41.820
osteoarthritis of the knee.

00:06:42.540 --> 00:06:45.240
Osteoarthritis patients
randomized to get

00:06:45.240 --> 00:06:47.340
about a pint and a half
of strawberries a day

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:48.060
for 12 weeks,

00:06:48.060 --> 00:06:51.420
and not only did
inflammatory markers plummet,

00:06:51.420 --> 00:06:54.840
they experienced significant
reductions in constant pain,

00:06:54.840 --> 00:06:58.440
intermittent pain,
and total pain.

00:06:58.440 --> 00:07:01.260
The first clinical study
of the effects of berries

00:07:01.260 --> 00:07:04.980
on human arthritis found that
a simple dietary intervention

00:07:04.980 --> 00:07:07.740
could have
a significant impact on pain,

00:07:07.740 --> 00:07:10.440
inflammation,
and overall quality of life.

00:07:10.440 --> 00:07:14.040
Surprisingly, blueberries didn't
seem to have the same effect.

00:07:14.040 --> 00:07:16.740
Despite the spin
in the title,

00:07:16.740 --> 00:07:19.200
twelve weeks of about four
servings of blueberries a day

00:07:19.200 --> 00:07:21.900
had no significant benefit
compared to placebo.

00:07:21.900 --> 00:07:26.040
They used conventional
(highbush) blueberries, though,

00:07:26.040 --> 00:07:27.960
which tend to have
less antioxidant power

00:07:27.960 --> 00:07:28.800
than strawberries

00:07:28.800 --> 00:07:31.440
and significantly less
antioxidant

00:07:31.440 --> 00:07:33.060
and anti-inflammatory activity

00:07:33.060 --> 00:07:36.000
compared to wild,
or lowbush, blueberries.

